*New collective bargaining agreement addressing BLOCKING CONDITIONS effective a of 3rd Feb 2024* 

* Platforms’ and drivers’ associations / unions agreed on rules related to drivers’ deactivation, including compensation in case the platform was proven liable for an unfair deactivation.
* Requirements are applicable *both to independent drivers and fleets drivers.* (Taxi category is out of scope though) and main obligations are: 

# *enhance transparency* and provide Drivers with clear information (on top of T&Cs) about blocking conditions and available rights/remedies;
# ensure that an *individual reviews each case before the Driver is blocked* and regardless of Driver's right to contest the decision (temporary suspension does not require prior human review though);
# *notify Drivers by email* prior/upon suspension, termination and each breach of T&Cs that could entail suspension/termination if repeated;
# *grant compensation* if the driver was erroneously blocked by the platform;
# put in place a "*reactivation committee"* that Drivers can invoke t*o be reinstated on the platform* if they fulfil specific requirements.

*Attached is an executive summary outlining efforts carried out at Bolt to ensure compliance* [https://docs.google.com/document/d/15vLomRurw8KlolNjJ0Uim_FLoCPm65GfZ3mg1nTDuj0/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/15vLomRurw8KlolNjJ0Uim_FLoCPm65GfZ3mg1nTDuj0/edit|smart-link]

