{color:#bf2600}*One concern related to ePrivacy Directive Art.5(3) exception for session cookies:*{color}

* As the auth_token is stored on the user’s device and then will be retrieved for cross app log-in, this operation falls into ePrivacy Directive (Art. 5(3)). For log-in we rely on the exception as storing auth_token is necessary to keep the user logged in for the session. However, as we can store the auth_token for a long time, this exception requires to have a consent. 
* One possible solution is to implement the button during the log-in 'Remember me”. This will explain that the user would be logged in until explicitly logged out + give an option to cross app log in to the Food app. 



{color:#bf2600}*Other implementations:*{color}

* *Agreed with Anamaria:* We would need to inform users that if they’re logged in one app, they can be logged in another app automatically without any SMS code needed _(if they agreed to click on remember me)_
* *Agreed with Anamaria:* We would need to inform users before the log-out that this would happen for the other app as well.

