Hi [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] 

Thank you so much for your comments  🙏 

{quote}I will mention this launch to the local counsel in those markets but in the meantime, are the timings on the confluence page still the proposed timings?{quote}

We intend to start testing within the time range mentioned in the document, but the exact rollout date is not critical for us. If we need more time from the Legal perspective to update the T&C, we can postpone the rollout. 

From your comment I see that we have to postpone the rollout in NL and FR - this is totally fine. Do you have any ETA for the T&C update? I’ll modify the schedule accordingly. 

One more question - we decided to replace Latvia to Finland due to the setup specifics in Latvia. Is it okay to roll out in FI without the T&C update?

{quote}I anticipate this will already have been foreseen / accommodated, but the feature cannot obviously be introduced to any driver that is a ‘true fleet driver’ (e.g. where the fleet driver gets paid by the fleet).{quote}

Absolutely, we plan to roll out the feature for the individual drivers only. 

{quote}In all ‘standard agency model markets’ we should only pass over cash via Early Cashouts if it has cleared in our accounts.{quote}

Could you please specify what do “cleared” funds mean? As far as I understand, according to our contract with Adyen, the funds are considered cleared as soon as the in-app payment is captured (i. e. immediately in the most part of the cases). The exception is failed payments, which we still cover for the driver.

Also, [~accountid:5b4c96fbda498c2c21cb8544] mentioned that this is more a balance than a payout problem - our team just pays out the funds that have been allocated to the balance. (See also [~accountid:624469dd45ece00069c967bd] 's comment). 

{quote}There is no absolute rule to follow here, but I understand that our fees are generally less than 1% of the average cashout which suggests to me that we are the right side of the line.{quote}

This should be fine - we can guarantee that the fee will be reasonable (<1%) and we will monitor it. 

{quote}From the tax side, our internal tax team needs to confirm the applicable rate of VAT that applies to our charges (if any).{quote}

We have discussed this with [~accountid:607d9ec5a41c7a007832afa1] and came to a conclusion that no changes are needed ([~accountid:607d9ec5a41c7a007832afa1] , pease correct me if I’m wrong). 

The invoices are currently issued monthly, but the Cashouts and the Cashout fee are correctly reflected.

{quote}In particular, we must avoid suggesting that we are giving anyone an ‘advancement of wages’{quote}

We normally communicate that the drivers can access their funds (i. e. already earned money) earlier than usual. 

Please let me know if I need to provide any additional documents/clarifications 🙏  If not, we will start preparing for testing and rollout in Estonia and Lithuania, and wait for your updates regarding Netherlands, France, and Finland.

Hello, [~accountid:5f6ba7e53672f3006a3b6cf0]!

* The draft lease agreement does not provide for any grace period in case of our delay in the payment of rent / electricity bills / related late payment penalties – I would suggest adding such grace period as it might happen that due to organizational error we will forget/fail to pay on time;
* Current draft does not regulate the rules of payment for the utilities (electricity, water, etc.), respective part of Article 25 has been deleted and at the same time delay in the payment for electricity gives the Landlord the right to early terminate our lease. It would be good to add such regulation to make sure that we know for which utilities we need to pay and that the landlord does not charge us with excessive fees.

